{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PUSHED — Gerrit 1331. Rebased onto current main first; a32a was NOT reverted.\n\nThe split was committed as `76fcaa414c` and sat unpushed. Before pushing I re-verified the base,\nbecause this change is the one that nearly reverted merged work once already (it branched\npre-1324, and because the refactor MOVES `get_parent_map` into a new file, a cherry-pick would\nhave applied clean).\n\n**Base check, and it was one commit stale AGAIN:**\n * `git merge-base --is-ancestor 2c71463b1e HEAD` -> YES (9bb9 intact, the original hazard)\n * but `HEAD..gerrit/main` showed **`3f5880cea9` (a32a, comment dedup via the codec seam)** was\n   missing. Rebased onto `gerrit/main`; the rebase was clean and both are now ancestors.\n * Confirmed the two changes touch **disjoint files** — a32a is `outbound_comments.py` + two\n   tests; the split is `jira_datacenter/*` only — so there was no silent-revert risk either way.\n   Checked rather than assumed, since \"applies cleanly\" is exactly what the near-miss looked like.\n\n**Result of the split:** `transport.py` 799 -> **230** lines, five mixins (`_base` 157,\n`_issues` 170, `_people` 177, `_hierarchy` 154, `_links` 110), all above the 100-LOC floor the\nmodule-size policy sets for split products. The file is off the cap, so parent-related work can\nland in it again.\n\n**Gates on the REBASED tree** (not the agent's original base):\n * ruff clean, mypy 429 files, module-size gate 0 violations\n * `test_dc_inbound_epic_link_9bb9.py` — **7 passed** (the specific regression guard)\n * full unit suite — **7734 passed, 24 skipped**\n\n### BLOCKED ON LANDING, and not for a reason in this change\n\nGerrit 1331 received `LLM-Review -1`, but it is a fail-closed infrastructure veto, not a finding:\n`llm-unavailable`, the bot's `base` step 403ing on Bedrock. Filed as\n[rebar:2322-da77-1281-402d] with the evidence. `Verified` has not voted yet. This change is ready\nand correct; it cannot land until the bot is healthy."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785805033426313001,"uuid":"6405e660-c39c-4350-bb2e-23d3ffdbcb9e"}